WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>Thanks for making time, Atul, Jahidi. I'd like to walk through how the pilot went and talk about what the full rollout could look like.</v>

2
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Atul Manohar>Sure. Overall the stores have been really positive. Staff picked it up faster than we expected.</v>

3
00:01:31.000 --> 00:02:01.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>Good to hear. On our side, the headline number is attach rate. Across the 50 pilot stores we're seeing a 9% attach-rate lift on smart-home bundles compared with the control stores.</v>

4
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:43.000
<v Atul Manohar>That matches what our store managers are telling me. The demo stations especially are pulling people in.</v>

5
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:23.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>So the proposal for next month is to take Aurora to all 400 stores ahead of the holiday season.</v>

6
00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:10.000
<v Atul Manohar>That's where I need to be straight with you. We've had Boulder Innovations in as well, and they quoted about 20% under your list price.</v>

7
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:58.000
<v Atul Manohar>If you can get close to that we could sign this quarter. I'd rather stay with Aurora, the pilot has gone well, but price is going to come up.</v>

8
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:36.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>Understood. Is that 20% on the hub alone, or does it include install and support?</v>

9
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:13.000
<v Atul Manohar>Honestly I'm not sure. I've only seen the per-store number, about $2,400.</v>

10
00:06:38.000 --> 00:07:09.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>That's in line with what we've seen from Boulder at other retailers. The $2,400 is the hub only. Once their install and support are added, it usually lands around $3,250 per store all-in.</v>

11
00:07:34.000 --> 00:08:03.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>So rather than match the 20%, here's what I can put forward: we hold the discount to 12%, that's $2,640 per store against our $3,000 list, and we bundle install at no extra cost.</v>

12
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:58.000
<v Atul Manohar>That's a better conversation than the sticker price. And Nanami will want the all-in cost. She's joining the pitch, and she'll look at the total for 400 stores, not the sticker price.</v>

13
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:35.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>That's helpful. I'll bring an all-in, per-store and total view for Nanami.</v>

14
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:30.000
<v Jahidi Juma>From the IT side, one thing before we go any further. We need a security review before the 400-store rollout. The pilot was a small footprint, so we let it through on a lighter check.</v>

15
00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:17.000
<v Jahidi Juma>For 400 stores I need to see your security documentation, where the data is stored, and confirm nothing captures customer PII in store.</v>

16
00:11:42.000 --> 00:12:02.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>Absolutely. We have a security and compliance FAQ, and I can set up a session with our team to walk through it with you.</v>

17
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:40.000
<v Jahidi Juma>That works. As long as it happens before anything is signed for the full rollout.</v>

18
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:30.000
<v Atul Manohar>One more thing from the stores: the reconnect issue we saw a couple of times. I'll send details separately, but it's not a blocker for this conversation.</v>

19
00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:16.000
<v Emil Vanggaard>Noted. So next steps: I'll set up the security review with Jahidi, and I'll come to the pitch with the all-in cost for Nanami.</v>

20
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:49.000
<v Atul Manohar>Sounds good. Thanks, Emil.</v>

21
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:22.000
<v Jahidi Juma>Thanks.</v>
